{
  "_comment": [
    "The predictor inputs for each kernel in src/, alongside the golden",
    "synthesis output under golden/<vitis-version>.json. Held as data, not",
    "as code in a test, because validating a new tool version means",
    "replaying exactly these inputs against that version's output \u2014 two",
    "copies of the argument lists would make that comparison meaningless",
    "the first time they drifted. See forge/hls/tool_matrix.py.",
    "",
    "unpredicted_prefixes / unpredicted_widths record what the predictor",
    "documented_gaps record what the predictor is known NOT to reproduce for",
    "this kernel, each with the reason. A difference they cover is accounted",
    "for; anything else is a real divergence for that tool version."
  ],
  "m_scalars": {
    "block_protocol": "ap_ctrl_none",
    "arguments": [
      {
        "name": "in_none",
        "width": 12,
        "mode": "ap_none"
      },
      {
        "name": "in_vld",
        "width": 12,
        "mode": "ap_vld"
      },
      {
        "name": "in_ack",
        "width": 12,
        "mode": "ap_ack"
      },
      {
        "name": "in_hs",
        "width": 12,
        "mode": "ap_hs"
      },
      {
        "name": "in_stable",
        "width": 12,
        "mode": "ap_stable"
      },
      {
        "name": "in_signed",
        "width": 8,
        "mode": "ap_none"
      },
      {
        "name": "out_none",
        "width": 12,
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "ap_none"
      },
      {
        "name": "out_vld",
        "width": 12,
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "ap_vld"
      },
      {
        "name": "out_ack",
        "width": 12,
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "ap_ack"
      },
      {
        "name": "out_hs",
        "width": 12,
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "ap_hs"
      }
    ]
  },
  "m_arrays": {
    "block_protocol": "ap_ctrl_hs",
    "returns_value": true,
    "return_width": 48,
    "arguments": [
      {
        "name": "grid_full",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          3,
          4
        ],
        "mode": "ap_none",
        "partition_dim": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "grid_dim1",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          3,
          4
        ],
        "partition_dim": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "line_mem",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "line_fifo",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          4
        ],
        "mode": "ap_fifo"
      },
      {
        "name": "st_in",
        "width": 48,
        "is_struct": true,
        "mode": "ap_none"
      },
      {
        "name": "line_out",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          4
        ],
        "is_output": true
      }
    ]
  },
  "m_axi": {
    "block_protocol": "ap_ctrl_hs",
    "arguments": [
      {
        "name": "strm_in",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          1
        ],
        "mode": "axis"
      },
      {
        "name": "strm_out",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          1
        ],
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "axis"
      },
      {
        "name": "cfg_a",
        "width": 12,
        "mode": "s_axilite"
      },
      {
        "name": "status_b",
        "width": 12,
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "s_axilite"
      },
      {
        "name": "mem",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          4
        ],
        "mode": "m_axi"
      }
    ],
    "documented_gaps": [
      {
        "reason": "s_axilite and m_axi bundles are not predicted: their port sets depend on address and data widths chosen at synthesis (see forge/hls/port_prediction.py's module docstring)",
        "prefixes": [
          "s_axi_",
          "m_axi_"
        ],
        "ports": [
          "interrupt"
        ]
      },
      {
        "reason": "with `s_axilite port=return`, block control moves into the AXI-Lite register map \u2014 HLS emits no ap_start/ap_done/ap_idle/ap_ready pins at all, which follows from the same s_axilite bundle this predictor does not model",
        "ports": [
          "ap_start",
          "ap_done",
          "ap_idle",
          "ap_ready"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "m_structs": {
    "block_protocol": "ap_ctrl_none",
    "returns_value": true,
    "return_width": 48,
    "arguments": [
      {
        "name": "as_scalar",
        "width": 48,
        "is_struct": true,
        "mode": "ap_none"
      },
      {
        "name": "as_array_elem",
        "width": 16,
        "dims": [
          2,
          2
        ],
        "is_struct": true,
        "mode": "ap_none",
        "partition_dim": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "o",
        "width": 12,
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "ap_vld"
      }
    ],
    "documented_gaps": [
      {
        "reason": "this kernel synthesised with no ap_clk pin at all, while keeping ap_rst; the predictor emits ap_clk unconditionally. What makes HLS drop the clock here is not established by one sample, so the difference is recorded rather than explained away",
        "ports": [
          "ap_clk"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "m_dimdefault": {
    "block_protocol": "ap_ctrl_none",
    "arguments": [
      {
        "name": "a_bare",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          3,
          4
        ],
        "partition_dim": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "b_dim0",
        "width": 12,
        "dims": [
          3,
          4
        ],
        "mode": "ap_none",
        "partition_dim": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "out",
        "width": 12,
        "is_output": true,
        "mode": "ap_vld"
      }
    ],
    "documented_gaps": [
      {
        "reason": "HLS inferred a dual-port memory for the dim=1-partitioned array (a second _address1/_ce1/_q1 set). How many memory ports it infers depends on the access pattern in the function body, which a signature-and-pragma predictor does not read",
        "ports": [
          "a_bare_0_address1",
          "a_bare_0_ce1",
          "a_bare_0_q1",
          "a_bare_1_address1",
          "a_bare_1_ce1",
          "a_bare_1_q1",
          "a_bare_2_address1",
          "a_bare_2_ce1",
          "a_bare_2_q1"
        ]
      },
      {
        "reason": "HLS renamed the scalar output `out` to `out_r`. One sample does not establish the rule (`out` is a VHDL reserved word and HLS emits VHDL as well as Verilog), so the rename is recorded here rather than turned into a naming rule the predictor applies to every port",
        "ports": [
          "out",
          "out_ap_vld",
          "out_r",
          "out_r_ap_vld"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
